 [RFC 6901 JSON Pointer](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901). An empty pointer selects the
 whole document. Non-empty pointers must begin with `/`; `~0` represents `~` and `~1` represents
 `/`. The function throws when the pointer is malformed or does not identify a value.
+
+## JSON Patch
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies an [RFC 6902 JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902)
+array using the `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, and `test` operations. It returns a new
+JSON value and never mutates the source document. Invalid patch documents and failed operations throw.
